course: dictionary
lesson: 2783
title: Dishonestly: not honest, by cheating
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dishonestly is an adverb, so it tells you how someone did something. It means in a way that is not honest, by lying, cheating or stealing. Honest means truthful and fair. Add dis- to show the opposite, and you get dishonestly.
explain: Context clues help you. «Ben copied his neighbour's test answers and got top marks» does not say the word, but it shows that Ben did not earn his marks fairly. Ask yourself: did they play fair, or did they cheat?
explain: The example from the course is harder, but the brackets help: «After a falsified presidential election (one whose votes were counted dishonestly) in November 2004, hundreds of thousands protested peacefully on Kyiv's Maidan». The brackets explain the hard word for you: the votes were counted in an unfair way, on purpose.
fact: Dishonestly is an adverb: it tells how someone acted.
fact: «Dishonestly» means in a way that is not honest, by lying, cheating or stealing.
fact: In law, «obtained dishonestly» means got something with the intention of cheating someone or taking what is not yours.
fact: Phrases like «act dishonestly» and «behave dishonestly» often appear in stories, where villains act this way.
fact: Honest means truthful and fair, so dishonestly is its opposite.
exercise: «The votes were counted dishonestly, so many people protested.» What does dishonestly mean here? | Happily, in a big crowd | Very quickly, by counting fast | *In a way that is not honest, to cheat | Slowly, with great care
exercise: Ben copied his neighbour's answers and got top marks. How did Ben get his marks? | Bravely, in front of the class | Honestly, by working hard | *Dishonestly, by cheating | Quietly, without a pen
exercise: Which phrase means behaving in a way that is not honest? | *Behave dishonestly | Behave loudly | Behave honestly | Behave kindly
test: The thief obtained the money ___. | slowly | softly | happily | *dishonestly
test: Which word means the opposite of dishonestly? | Loudly | Carelessly | *Honestly | Quickly
exam: Read: «Sam said he had finished his homework, but he copied it dishonestly from a website.» What does dishonestly tell you about how Sam did his homework? | Quickly, in a rush | *By cheating, not doing his own work | Late, after the bell | Neatly, in his best handwriting
